  "mechanism": {
    "old": "At 51e820c1d, the multi-changed-ID branch replays changedIds for every selected label and calls nextSource with per-ID binary occurrence searches. The one-ID branch already streamed. This is repeated replay and point search, not a claim that each old nextSource rescanned every occurrence.",
    "new": "changedIds is consumed once. Each sourcesForId cursor walks call ordinals once and merges its reconstruction target. Up to 64 live label cursors use a deduplicating heap. A 65th nonempty cursor switches to scalar streaming through sortedLabels; neither changed IDs nor all holders are materialized in production.",
    "cascade": "A single pending identity displaces 129 historical IDs in the injected same-candidate fixture. This exceeds the cursor cap without making a history-sized heap or ID map. Exact occurrence count is 258, with old salt i and new salt i+1 for every historical ID.",
    "ordering": "The persistent fallback encodes labels as unsigned big-endian 64-bit prefixes in 16-byte keys, uses identity hashing and an existing IdFactBatch/IdTrieReader, and emits distinct keys in trie order. Heap and trie paths both deduplicate shared holder labels.",
    "complexityLimit": "This removes per-holder repair replay. It does not establish linear total collision resolution: the deliberate same-candidate salt adversary still requires candidate retries, reflected in the 17548 fact lookups. No suffix-replay fallback or legitimate-input unsupported guard was introduced."
  },
  "sourceLines": {
    "packages/core/src/services/history/mistral-source-merge.ts": "4-83: fixed cursor cap, fallback and finally cleanup",
    "packages/core/src/services/history/journal-request-mistral.ts": "90-162: tail-sized repair frontier; 165-210: sequential holders and merge; 213-277: charged mapping cache and cursor",
    "packages/core/src/journal/ordered-labels.ts": "15-82: pinned serialized persistent sorting and final release",
    "packages/core/src/journal/idFactBatch.ts": "52-63,174-195,202-208: charged spill batch",
    "packages/core/src/journal/idTrieReader.ts": "91-115: one trie path, shared node cache",
    "packages/core/src/journal/journalStore.ts": "514-531: snapshot and sorter admission wiring"
  },
  "stateAndCapacity": {
    "cursors": "At most 64 heap entries plus the admitted 65th source generator; the readers set is fixed at at most 65. All use the snapshot fact reader, not a separate ROW reader/cache per historical ID.",
    "tail": "For P seed identities, each repair removes one frontier before inserting at most one displaced owner. Terminal IDs grow only when a frontier ends. Frontier/terminal count is at most P, not historical cascade length; seed and identifier byte sizes remain input-dependent.",
    "mappingCacheChargedBytes": 65536,
    "scalarSpill": "Each empty-valued key charges 16+480=496 bytes. The >65536 threshold flushes after at most 133 entries (65968 charged bytes), not a claimed 128-entry buffer. Sorting also holds a fixed chunk-sized array. The batch readback and final trie reader each have 64 KiB charged node caches; the group appender has its existing 256 KiB buffer. These individual caps are not a whole-heap measurement.",
    "triePath": "128-bit keys and four-bit levels bound a traversal path to 32 levels; leaves hold at most eight entries.",
    "disk": "Fallback writes one committed group through the existing persistent descriptor. Scratch trie roots are unreachable from published history; durableEnd increases while published roots and aggregate/liveBytes remain unchanged. Written and superseded nodes are journal garbage, subject to existing pinned compaction, not zero storage. At 129 cascaded IDs the measured extra durable bytes are 9120; at two IDs they are zero. No aggregate or 100000-call capacity acceptance is inferred.",
    "rowWindow": "Existing shared ROW reader retains 32768 bytes with a 49152-byte replacement transient in the measured warm fixture. Decoded-holder WeakRef coverage is separate from complete retained heap; no history-sized array is permitted in production.",
    "finally": "Merge finally returns admitted readers and changed iterator; sorter finally releases its pinned descriptor. New sorter tests preserve original input-error identity and close after early consumer stop. Existing #3919 suites pass 11/29 and 3/20, without assertion or production changes."
  },
